IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fwa-employee`

-- Fair Work Act 2009 (with the Fair Work Regulations 2009), the employee's and the platform worker's questions -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_fair-work-act-2009_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Facts are from the three Western Australian lives (workbench scenarios/au/wa/cradle-to-grave-*), named by event id in
-- each fixture or comment. Figures marked HYPOTHETICAL are invented for the case and are not the real amounts.

`Jake riding for the platform (k040)` MEANS PlatformWork WITH
    `I am an individual party to the services contract and do the work` IS TRUE
    `I do all or a significant majority of the work` IS TRUE
    `the work is paid and done through a digital labour platform` IS TRUE
    `I do some of the work as an employee` IS FALSE
    `I have low bargaining power` IS TRUE
    `I am paid at or below a comparable employee` IS FALSE
    `I have little authority over how I do the work` IS TRUE
    `I have a prescribed characteristic` IS FALSE

`a rider with only low bargaining power` MEANS PlatformWork WITH
    `I am an individual party to the services contract and do the work` IS TRUE
    `I do all or a significant majority of the work` IS TRUE
    `the work is paid and done through a digital labour platform` IS TRUE
    `I do some of the work as an employee` IS FALSE
    `I have low bargaining power` IS TRUE
    `I am paid at or below a comparable employee` IS FALSE
    `I have little authority over how I do the work` IS FALSE
    `I have a prescribed characteristic` IS FALSE

